					<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Welcome!
					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Thu, Jul 01, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Hey guys, welcome to the new site.
<br />

<br />
A few quick things I want to mention:
<br />

<br />
1) This site is completely skinnable.  I'm aware that a lot of people are not too keen on the green/purple theme, but I created it to give the site some character.  You can change to a black/red theme that matches the general look/feel of the old site by logging in and then selecting "Change Site Theme" from the menu.
<br />

<br />
If you are interested in creating a skin for the site, please contact me via PM (this forum or the EQ one) or e-mail at <a href="mailto:thenexus@gotteverquest.net">TheNexus@gotteverquest.net</a>.
<br />

<br />
2) I will be reading the forum suggestion box pretty regularly and reading them, so feel free to make any suggestions you want, including feature requests and I'll do what I can to fulfill them.  Feel free to put in suggestions for new site skins too if you like, since me and probably Daisy and Kalect will be working on skins from time to time.  ^_^
<br />

<br />
3) I will be on EQIM whenever I'm not online, so once you have signed up on this site please send me a tell in-game with your character names and your username from this site, so that I can properly promote you and associate your username with your characters on the new roster.
<br />

<br />
4) Once you are properly promoted to Guild Member on the site you will have access to the guild calendar and the member-only forums.  There will probably be some functions to be added at a later time as well.
<br />

<br />

					<p>-- TheNexus
</p>
			</td></tr>
			</table><br />	
					<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					NEW WEBSITE!
					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Thu, Jul 01, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Ok, I'm sorry, I haven't updated in a while, but for the most part, there 
hasn't been much going on.  However, there are some recent changes that 
need to be noted, so I am updating now.<br /><br />

1. Lore and links sections added to the websites.<br /><br />

The lore section was added to create a giant compendium of lore and news, 
so that the Guardians would never be left in the dark about the history of 
Norrath nor the current events.  Please check it out, I have more detailed 
information there.<br /><br />

The links section is rather obvious.  Send me a message for suggestions of 
links.<br /><br />

2. New Website<br /><br />

As fond as you all are of this site, we have a new one.  A few more 
technical difficulties need to be worked out, but for the most part it is 
fully operational.  Go to <a 
href="http://guild.shadowfury.net/">http://guild.shadowfury.net</a> and 
sign up today!  The projected transfer date is July 9, 2004.  I have been 
working with TheNexus and Kalect to get all the pieces arranged.<br /><br />

The new site has a much greater functionality, and more ability to adjust 
to meet our needs.  Links will be set up to view the guildportal page of 
Rivals of the Throne, our sister roleplay guild.<br /><br />

3. Magelo Links<br /><br />

I understand that many of you don't want to pay for the Magelo premium 
service, but I still recommend getting Magelo Update (available at <a 
href="http://www.magelo.com/">http://www.magelo.com</a>) and at least 
building your Magelo profiles.  If you do have Magelo premium service, I 
suggest using it to automatically build your character profiles.  The 
ability to see what others want and need is a great boon to our 
community.<br /><br />

4. Guild Events<br /><br />

We have a drunken race set up from Qeynos to Freeport on July 10, 2004.  
It is currently set up for running at Noon EDT, but the time is always 
subject to meet the needs of the players.  Since Daisy posted it, I would 
assume that she would like to participate.  This is for members of both 
guilds.  Remember, Daisy is six hours ahead of EDT, so please remember 
this when you suggest a time.<br /><br />

RoTT, our rival and sister Guild, is on the rise.  Rumor has it that it is 
led by a certain Pirate.  Watch out for them!  My sources tell me that 
they are out to capture the Princess!  We must defend her at all 
costs!<br /><br />

5. Other information<br /><br />

Don't forget to use /autojoin princesslakotah followed by /join 
princesslakotah every time you make a new character.  It cuts down on the 
hassle of joining the chat channel every time you log in on that 
character.<br /><br />

Questions? Comments?  Concerns?  I can always be reached at <a 
href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>.  
I have been checking my email every day.  You can also use the EQ message 
boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.


					<p>-- Coar
</p>
			</td></tr>
