					<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Hail, Adventurers of Norrath! Welcome back, fellow guardians!
					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Tue, Jun 08, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Wow, its been a while since i updated this. Oh well. I've kinda had alot going on, and most of my free time has been used talking to my gorgeous girlfriend, our guild leader, the Princess Lakotah. Well, that and EQ of course (its cheapest to talk there, never worry about cell phone minutes).<br />
<br />
Hmm... recent events....<br />
<br />
GoTT Fight Night got converted into a giant language lesson due to low numbers, that or the idea kinda died. But it was fun anyway, and a good time was had by all!<br />
<br />
Due to scheduling problems, Daisy, the Spacy Haarlem Hottie, has had trouble playing with us here in the US due to the fact that she is 6 hours ahead of EDT. Our 6pm is her midnight. I'd like to know what your average schedule is, so that we can try to plan guild events when most, if not all, can participate. (Hopefully I'll be able to arrange the next event as the Daisy and Kotah Show's first episode... no promises though... :) )<br />
<br />
Also, for those of you who want to donate to the guild bank, just let an officer know what it is and that you want it to go to the guild bank. You can trust any of them to be honest about your donations, which will go to the guild banker, one of the alts on my 3rd account. Currently, Kotah has donated a pair of boots (kinda, still don't have em to update the site) and Aukin has made a generous donation (he requested that the amount be unlisted) for people that need some money to help get all their spells. As listed in the thread covering this issue here on our own boards, please try to buy them on your own, and use guild funds as an alternate, but we do want you to have all of the spells for your level, just use your best judgement.<br />
Questions? Comments? Concerns? I can always be reached at <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>. I have been checking my email every day. You can also use the EQ Message boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.
					<p>-- Coar
</p>
			</td></tr>
